(5) Necessity
    c = tau: reference (0,10), M = {(0,10),(10,0)}, tau = 1, g = 0: the point at length 10 ties, so no
    length bound holds at c = tau; at c = 1.01 the bound l <= 0 holds.
    margin: an N-point with J'_c equal to the reference value is near-optimal at eps = 0, so the margin
    must be strict, as stated.
